## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design an incremental data structure for computing a non-trivial graph statistic under streaming batch updates.

## Key Concepts
- Incremental degree-based metrics
- Amortized analysis for batch/streaming updates
- Space-time trade-offs in dynamic graph algorithms

## Code Example
```javascript
let deg = Array(n).fill(0);
let P = 0;

function addEdge(u, v) {
  const du = deg[u], dv = deg[v];
  P += 2 * (du + dv);
  deg[u] = du + 1;
  deg[v] = dv + 1;
}

function processBatch(edges) {
  edges.forEach(([u, v]) => addEdge(u, v));
  return P;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle edge deletions?
- How does multi-graph handling (parallel edges) affect this approach?
- What are the time and space complexities compared to recomputing from scratch?

